                                "sense_id": "225e036b-31de-3d1a-a749-508d02544fd7",
                                "text": "In the 1890’s “women were behind the stove,” he relates. But they cycled, too. “And they had difficulty pedalling bicycles with ankle-length skirts. “At the time,” Taylor said, “the most sinful thing a woman could do was to show light between her legs. “The original culotte was designed by a LAW member’s wife. The churches (in the East) termed this bepantsed female activity of biking “sinful bicycling,” he noted."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "460d380d-afce-420f-887c-7d574cabcfef",
                                "sense_id": "225e036b-31de-3d1a-a749-508d02544fd7",
                                "text": "It was as if she had that morning been transferred back over forty years to her youth again, and was having the good times that she had longed for, such as other girls had—the swings, and the rides, and the skatings, and bicyclings."
                            }
